    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23-a1">

                <pb facs="0156" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg32"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 411.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kasson to Baron Haymerle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 31,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United
                    States of America, referring to the from the foreign office (I, 1475–9), under
                    date of August 4, 1880, announcing that one Marcus Cohn, had renounced his
                    American citizenship, and assumed that of Austria, begs that his excellency
                    Baron Haymerle, minister of the imperial house and imperial and royal minister
                    for foreign affairs, will be so good as to cause the transmission to this
                    legation, of a statement which will certify the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >place</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">time</hi> of this act of
                    renunciation by the aforesaid Cohn, together with a copy of the record of the
                    same showing the <hi rendition="#italic">formal act</hi> of renunciation,
                    certificate of which appears to be required for use in the United States.</p>
                <p>The undersigned will also be glad to receive, for the information of the
                    Department <pb facs="0157" n="33" xml:id="pg33"/> of State at Washington, a copy
                    of the law, if any, under which such acts of renunciation are recorded.</p>
                <p>He avails himself of this occasion to renew to his excellency Baron Haymerle, the
                    assurance of his very distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>KASSON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His excellency, Baron <hi rendition="#small-caps">Haymerle</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
